"""BLAS/linalg type surface — `LinalgError`, `NormOrd`, `BlasHandle` (T-BLAS-01).

This is the single definition site for the scilib BLAS type and handle
surface.  It was extracted out of `blas.spl` so the handle policy lives with
the handle rather than in a module comment on the provider file.  `blas.spl`
keeps the arithmetic (MockCpuBlasProvider and the `blas_*_f64` wrappers) and
references this file for the policy.

Layer note: `BlasHandle` carries no primitive in its public signature — the
raw `cublasHandle_t` is a Layer A concern (`ffi_blas.spl`) and never surfaces
here.

Import path: use std.common.science_math.types.{NormOrd, LinalgError, BlasHandle}

# THREAD-SAFETY: one handle per process in v1; actor boundary crossing forbidden.
# `cublasHandle_t` is per-thread (NVIDIA recommendation), so v1 pins exactly one
# module-level BlasHandle and forbids passing it across a `nogc_async_mut` actor
# boundary without an explicit lock.  v1.1 will revisit once actor-aware
# handle-per-fiber is designed.  This paragraph is the authority; every other
# thread-safety comment in the area points here.
"""

# ============================================================
# NormOrd — used by the linalg.norm public API
# ============================================================

pub enum NormOrd:
    L1
    L2
    Inf

# ============================================================
# Extended LinalgError
# (subset shared with the lapack area; coordinate on final definition location)
# ============================================================

pub enum LinalgError:
    Singular
    DimensionMismatch
    UnsupportedDType(text)
    BackendUnavailable(text)

# ============================================================
# BlasHandle
#
# LP64 ABI only in v1; ILP64 documented as a later extension.
# Provider selection order: mock -> scalar -> openblas -> cublas.  In v1 the
# handle always names the pure-Simple mock path, so no Layer A handle is
# allocated and there is nothing to destroy; `ffi_blas.blas_handle_create`
# is the Layer A entry point v1.1 will bind here.
# See the THREAD-SAFETY paragraph in this file's docstring before sharing one.
# ============================================================

pub class BlasHandle:
    backend: text

    pub static fn create() -> BlasHandle:
        BlasHandle(backend: "mock")

    pub fn backend_name(self) -> text:
        self.backend
